{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeZEbasgojp4pB3ML7ghg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The page's only real defect was a single blanket rule that suppressed all focus indicators (`*:focus { outline: none }`), which is a WCAG 2.4.7 (Focus Visible) failure. Every interactive element on the page — the nav links, the search input, the search button, and the two `data-track` buttons — is already a native, semantic, keyboard-operable element (`<a>`, `<input>`, `<button>`), so no structural or ARIA remediation was needed; keyboard users could already Tab to and activate everything, they just couldn't *see* where focus was.\n\n**Change made:**\n- Removed the global `*:focus { outline: none }` rule.\n- Added a scoped, visible focus style (`a:focus-visible, button:focus-visible, input:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #2456c4; outline-offset: 2px; }`) using the site's existing blue accent color, so focus is clearly visible without altering the visual design in any other state.\n\n**Left alone (already compliant):**\n- All `data-track` attributes and `id`s, kept on their original elements.\n- The instrumentation script, untouched.\n- Semantic structure (`header`, `nav`, `main`, single `h1`), existing `aria-label` on the search input, and text/color contrast, all of which already met AA.\n- No widget swaps were needed since every control was already a native element with correct semantics and mouse/keyboard parity."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":790,"cache_read_input_tokens":11779,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":790},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b3844211-2f75-45c3-bb12-0f2c9c379779","uuid":"0078d801-dd09-422a-aeca-68b5f3b8815e","timestamp":"